WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.455
Part seven.

00:00:01.455 --> 00:00:03.825
Export the scenario as test code.

00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:09.101
Once a scenario is solid, you can turn it into real test code for your CI.

00:00:09.101 --> 00:00:13.233
Open the Tools tab, go to Export Code, and choose Buy a book.

00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:17.997
Selenium Python: a script that runs as is, or a pytest test.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.189
Each step becomes a block of code commented with its name, with every locator it has, tried in turn.

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:28.513
Variables, Conditions and Read DOM all turn into matching code.

00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:34.757
The Settings tab sets the start URL, the browser and headless mode, and the code updates instantly.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.306
Copy it, or download it as a file.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:51.391
There's also Playwright Test, Robot Framework, Selenium Java for TestNG, and a JavaScript bookmarklet that runs without the extension.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.417
Not every step exports as is.

00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:09.547
The Actions tab marks each one: OK when it exports, Verify when you should check it by hand, and Skip when it can't be exported.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:17.664
For example, a bookmarklet can't upload files: in Update profile, the upload step is marked Skip.

00:01:17.664 --> 00:01:22.358
Click it to see the comment left in its place, so nothing goes missing silently.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.831
Next, a tool for when you read documentation: Highlights.
